KG42.register("slice-clusters-3ef358e7cf8ff827f824be8b",{"id":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v142-d-K001","paper":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives","title":"Regulated electricity-price feedback and investment scheduling under coalition branches","source_pointer":"/clusters/64","node_ids":["COMP-0f9c791362e86686","COMP-259000fdd3b58453","COMP-13ec024ac7c1d3de","COMP-11593fa2cb05bce9"],"rule_refs":["16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R001","16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R002","16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R003","16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R004"],"visible_rule_refs":["16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R001","16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R002","16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R003","16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R004"],"suppressed_rule_refs":[],"edges":[{"global_edge_id":"S-f65b9bfe39f9752a","source":"COMP-259000fdd3b58453","target":"COMP-0f9c791362e86686","type":"links","assertion_ids":["16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R001::E::v141-c-R001-E001"],"rule_refs":["16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R001"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-980a1f0c9175650e","source":"COMP-259000fdd3b58453","target":"COMP-13ec024ac7c1d3de","type":"links","assertion_ids":["16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E001"],"rule_refs":["16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R002"],"internal":false}],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"interface_annotations":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C008","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C009"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e027","v141-b-g04-E14","v141-b-g04-E15","v141-b-g04-E16"],"rationale":"The surplus objective of the same {Private investor, D} model is subject to distribution balance, reactive-power demand, and externally specified capacity-expansion constraints; the objective and feasibility region are complementary, but the existing constraints do not exhaust the model."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-E20","v141-b-g04-E21","v141-b-g04-E07","v141-b-g04-E10"],"rationale":"The grand-coalition model explicitly cites the distribution-balance and flow constraints that include export, so its objective can be associated with these existing constraints; this inheritance does not include the export prohibition of {Private investor, D}."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g05-e07","v141-b-g05-e08","v141-b-g05-e05"],"rationale":"The independent optimization procedure of the two-party consumer coalition has mutual feedback between MG quantity decisions and VIU price updates, connecting the local configuration with the fixed-point description; this does not constitute a convergence guarantee and does not add a scientific edge."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g05-e06","v141-b-g04-E24","v141-b-g04-E20","v141-b-g04-E21"],"rationale":"Within the grand-coalition scope shared by both parties, consumption response, scheduling solution, and price updating form the same numerical procedure; the other coalitions in R003 do not thereby acquire the grand-coalition objective of R002."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C010","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C011"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-E13","v141-b-g04-E14","v141-b-g04-E16","v141-b-g02-e027"],"rationale":"The imported-electricity expenditure of {Private investor, D} enters the joint objective directly, and the residents' supplementary heating expenditure is associated through gas use in the heat balance; this is a substantive interface between cost and quantity, and no precedence relation is inferred from the names activation and clearing."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X003","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X004","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-qe_MG_ljt","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-f_klt","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-f_lkt"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-E07","v141-b-g04-E10","v141-b-g04-E14","v141-b-g04-E16"],"rationale":"Within the same coalition, node, and time period, generation and bidirectional distribution flows connect the configuration and transaction representations. Export quantity is connected only in the branch that allows export, and the zero-export transcription of another branch cannot be used to cover all coalitions."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN007","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C007"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C006","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C008"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-E14","v141-b-g04-E16","v141-b-g04-E10","v141-b-g04-E12"],"rationale":"The two groups of references respectively duplicate Eq. (41) and Eq. (37) and are not counted as additional independent rules. The load-object roles in Eq. (41) are inconsistent, so they are kept parallel; the applicable coalition and mathematical content of Eq. (37) are consistent, so only a display-representative selection can be made."}],"annotation_policy":"Original D connections are annotations, not additional S edges.","empty_after_chain_suppression":false});
